  "id": "COMPOUND:23337 - PROTEIN:2718",
  "verbalization": "Nanolobatin B appears to interact with Triosephosphate isomerase through multiple indirect pathways, suggesting a broader role in modulating metabolic processes. The evidence indicates that Nanolobatin B targets different proteins, including the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit beta-2, Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, and Cyclin-dependent kinase 7, which in turn target Triosephosphate isomerase. These findings suggest that Nanolobatin B may exert its effects by influencing cellular processes that ultimately lead to the regulation of Triosephosphate isomerase, a key enzyme in glycolytic metabolism. The shared involvement of Triosephosphate isomerase across these pathways implies a potential functional link, though the exact mechanism by which Nanolobatin B modulates its activity remains to be elucidated. The integration of these relationships highlights the complexity of the metabolic network and underscores the importance of further investigation into the molecular interactions that underlie Nanolobatin B's effects.",
